# Compose UI

```kotlin
// ✅ existing pattern
@Composable
fun FooScreen(viewModel: FooViewModel, onX: () -> Unit) {
    val uiState by viewModel.uiState.collectAsState()
    FooScreenContent(
        uiState = uiState,
        onRetry = viewModel::refreshAll,
        onRefresh = viewModel::refreshAll,
        onX = onX,
    )
}

@Composable
fun FooScreenContent(uiState: FooUiState, onRetry: () -> Unit, /* callbacks */) { /* … */ }
```

- Split `*Screen` (collect + wire VM) from `*ScreenContent` (pure UI for androidTest).
- Branch on `AsyncValue`: Loading → shimmer; Error → `ErrorBody`; Value → content. Prefer existing components in `ui/components/`.
- Pull-to-refresh: `PullToRefreshBox` + VM `refreshAll` / `AppDataRefresh` — do not clear Room from the composable.
- Strings via `stringResource(R.string.*)`; typography/spacing via `AppStyles` / `AppDimens` / theme colors — avoid hard-coded copy and one-off text styles.
- Put screens under `ui/screens/<feature>/`; shared widgets in `ui/components/`. No Retrofit/DAO/Hilt construction in composables.
